+
+Pass `snapshotId` with `carryPolicy` (`--snapshot ID --carry JSON` in the CLI) to evaluate small carry bids against reserved cash and a holding hurdle. The policy requires `cases` containing `actionId`, conditional-on-full-fill `winProbabilityLow`/`winProbabilityHigh`, and `usableCashAtEarliest`/`usableCashAtLatest`. Optional `priorityReserveUsd` protects cash for better uses; `hourlyCashHurdle` is a dollar-per-dollar-per-hour opportunity cost; `minimumWinSurplusUsd` and `maxLossBudgetUsd` constrain selection. Captured resting actions are ranked greedily by conservative conditional net per dollar-hour; optimality and the conditional probability/cash-release assumptions remain unproved. The selected actions pass the existing shared-cash verifier using the residual budget. Allocation reads no venue data and does not refit weather models; its policy, evaluation and verifier result are retained through `weather_evidence`.
+
+A 97-cent bid does not imply a 97% conditional win probability. With a conservative one-cent fee reserve, winning returns two cents, but a 99% conditional win probability gives only one cent of expected net before opportunity cost. At 97% it gives minus one cent. On a fee-free cent-price contract the win surplus is three cents. Fee reserves now derive from the existing exact `scheduledFee` primitive: the venue rounds position cost plus fee to a centicent, and an integer-hundredth fragmentation bound replaces whole-cent rounding plus a blanket per-contract fragmentation overhead. The declared source patchset, precommitted cases, exact partition oracle, staged consumer receiving and failed first candidate are retained in `data/records/2026-10-07-weather-capital-opportunity`. Market close is not certified cash release; the scenario must supply that separate interval.
+
+
+
+Optional `carryPolicy.postedLossPolicy` supplies `{tailFraction, maxGrossExpectedShortfallUsd}`. Every case must then also supply a separate `marginalWinProbabilityLow` for the quoted side: the conditional-on-full-fill probability is never reused as this marginal. For worst-tail mass `a` (e.g. 0.05 for the worst 5%), the gross posted-loss envelope has expected shortfall at most `sum(cost_i * min(1, (1-pLow_i)/a))`, allowing any dependence among weather errors and fills, including partial fills bounded by the captured fee reserve. Opposite YES/NO marginal lower bounds for the same contract must sum to at most one; contradictory supplied bounds are refused. This cap consumes one portfolio budget during greedy selection and is retained in the normal participation evidence. It excludes winning profits and credits no collateral return. The bound is sharp only for unrestricted Bernoulli envelopes, can be loose for logically related weather contracts, and remains conditional on supplied marginal probabilities and costs; it supplies no calibration or order authority. See [Embrechts, Wang and Wang, Section 3](https://people.math.ethz.ch/~embrecht/ftp/agg_rob_2014_FS.pdf) and [Dhara, Das and Natarajan](https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.04167) for risk aggregation under unknown dependence.
+
+
+Reported-temperature metrology supplements the original point-temperature lane. `observedExtremes.temperatureMetrology` retains validated raw METAR whole-Celsius and tenths-Celsius inverse-rounding cells, their page hashes, actual receipts and conflicting witnesses. Numeric API formatting or observation cadence alone never establishes reporting precision; those rows remain unidentified. Cells cover reporting quantization, not instrument error or final climate extremes. The `paired-family-cell-ewa-v1` station experiment requires publication before the earliest possible target report (15 minutes before the target hour). It scores CRPS and paired component excess-loss ranges over the same source-supported cell, using exact empirical atoms and the existing 41-node Student-t scoring approximation. Prospective cell comparisons feed a separate past-only family learner using upper paired excess loss, equal date contributions, the existing fixed prior/rate/window and uniform share; it does not reuse point-label fits. `weather_station_skill` exposes `measurementMetrics`; full cell outcomes and model inputs remain in `weather_evidence`. Unknown or contradictory cells cannot supply a training label. The outcome uses the first received eligible report set; later arrivals or revisions remain source evidence and never rewrite that frozen outcome. Report-cell targets use `measurementPending` within the existing locked state record; older point-only consumers preserve that map but never interpret its targets. Known report-cell targets from the earlier candidate are migrated from `pending` under the same lock. Original forecasts, point scores and venue settlement remain separate. This is an uncalibrated experiment, with no regret or profitability claim. Primary measurement descriptions: [NWS Chicago](https://www.weather.gov/lot/weather_observations_faq), [NWS Los Angeles](https://www.weather.gov/lox/asostemperature).
